# Example tor configuration for putting onion-gate in front of a backend.
#
# The key line is HiddenServiceExportCircuitID haproxy: it makes tor prepend a
# PROXY v1 line to every connection, carrying a per-circuit identifier.
# onion-gate reads it (with --proxy-protocol) to apply its per-circuit limits.
# Without this line, onion-gate still works but can only apply the per-pass
# limit (every visitor looks like the same circuit).

HiddenServiceDir /var/lib/tor/onion-gate/
HiddenServiceVersion 3
# Visitors reach the .onion on port 80; tor forwards to onion-gate on loopback.
HiddenServicePort 80 127.0.0.1:8088
HiddenServiceExportCircuitID haproxy

# Optional hardening (recommended for a service that only serves a hidden
# service and makes no outbound connections of its own):
# SocksPort 0
# Keep onion-gate and the backend bound to 127.0.0.1 only.
